DECISIONS 332, 403, CODEGEN.md §7.9: the project's defines come from the packages it scans, and none is scanned under an absent optional root (nothing is there to read): b spells alpha, and the only package that could write it as a #define would live under the absent root @ext, so b is clean.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  roots {
    out: "out"
    ext: "ext"
  }
  optional_roots: [ext]
}
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// Tones.
enum Tone {
  /// Spelled like a define that is not scanned.
  alpha
}

emit cpp { out: "@out/b", namespace: "b", mode: types }
-- check-only --
-- select --
b
-- findings.txt --
0 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
